WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:02.234 --> 00:00:03.434
-Donald Trump called
on Republicans

00:00:03.434 --> 00:00:06.367
to defund the FBI and DOJ
after he was arrested

00:00:06.367 --> 00:00:08.534
and arraigned on
34 felony charges Tuesday.

00:00:08.534 --> 00:00:10.701
Meanwhile, Republicans
are threatening retaliation

00:00:10.701 --> 00:00:12.133
by openly admitting

00:00:12.133 --> 00:00:14.267
they'll use the justice system
to go after Joe Biden.

00:00:14.267 --> 00:00:16.300
For more on this, it's time
for A Closer Look.

00:00:16.300 --> 00:00:18.434
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:00:18.434 --> 00:00:20.501
♪♪

00:00:20.501 --> 00:00:23.467
Donald Trump's allies have spent
the last few days claiming Trump

00:00:23.467 --> 00:00:26.300
is actually enjoying the media
spectacle around his indictment

00:00:26.300 --> 00:00:27.868
and even the process

00:00:27.868 --> 00:00:29.400
of surrendering himself
for arrest.

00:00:29.400 --> 00:00:31.834
-Trump, for his part,
is reportedly

00:00:31.834 --> 00:00:35.000
downplaying his predicament
behind closed doors,

00:00:35.000 --> 00:00:36.701
according to a new story
in The New York Times,

00:00:36.701 --> 00:00:39.601
the former president
has told friends and associates

00:00:39.601 --> 00:00:42.601
that he welcomes the idea
of being paraded around

00:00:42.601 --> 00:00:45.567
by the authorities,
surrounded by the media.

00:00:45.567 --> 00:00:47.868
Trump has also reportedly
mused openly

00:00:47.868 --> 00:00:50.234
about whether to smile
for the cameras

00:00:50.234 --> 00:00:52.133
during a possible perp walk

00:00:52.133 --> 00:00:56.434
and described the potential
situation as a fun experience.

00:00:56.434 --> 00:00:59.501
-Oh, it's going to be a fun
experience is definitely a lie

00:00:59.501 --> 00:01:02.601
you tell people
when you were scared [bleep].

00:01:02.601 --> 00:01:05.267
That's 100% what I would say
right before skydiving.

00:01:05.267 --> 00:01:07.634
This is going to be so great.

00:01:07.634 --> 00:01:10.133
I just can't decide
if I'm going to smile or not.

00:01:10.133 --> 00:01:13.200
[ Laughter ]

00:01:13.200 --> 00:01:14.868
The only way you could
possibly find the experience

00:01:14.868 --> 00:01:17.234
of getting arrested fun
is if everything about your life

00:01:17.234 --> 00:01:18.267
is absolutely miserable,

00:01:18.267 --> 00:01:19.634
which I guess applies
to Donald Trump.

00:01:19.634 --> 00:01:21.667
I mean, look at him.
That was taken right after

00:01:21.667 --> 00:01:25.067
someone said they were free
donuts in the break room.

00:01:25.067 --> 00:01:26.701
The man is constantly enraged,

00:01:26.701 --> 00:01:28.300
and I know I'm wasting
my time saying this,

00:01:28.300 --> 00:01:30.567
but I think a person
describing a perp walk

00:01:30.567 --> 00:01:32.501
as a fun experience
is disqualifying

00:01:32.501 --> 00:01:33.801
for the office of president.

00:01:33.801 --> 00:01:36.234
So put that on my list
that nobody gives [bleep] about,

00:01:36.234 --> 00:01:38.667
right after stared at an eclipse
and right before called

00:01:38.667 --> 00:01:41.667
Apple CEO Tim Cook, Tim Apple.

00:01:41.667 --> 00:01:45.567
Nothing -- Nothing involving the
criminal justice system is fun.

00:01:45.567 --> 00:01:46.834
Oh, sure.
Oh, sure.

00:01:46.834 --> 00:01:48.534
You might think --
you might think it's fun to be

00:01:48.534 --> 00:01:50.667
one of the guys they bring in
to fill out a police lineup.

00:01:50.667 --> 00:01:51.801
Well, I used to do that

00:01:51.801 --> 00:01:53.067
for a little extra money
back in the day,

00:01:53.067 --> 00:01:55.334
and it was fun
till the day I got fingered

00:01:55.334 --> 00:01:57.834
for the liquor store
that B.J. Novak knocked over.

00:01:57.834 --> 00:02:00.100
[ Laughter ]

00:02:00.100 --> 00:02:01.834
Should have known it was him,
because you know

00:02:01.834 --> 00:02:03.968
what he did
to the security camera?

00:02:05.434 --> 00:02:07.534
[ Laughter ]

00:02:07.534 --> 00:02:08.634
Donald Trump thought
it would be fun

00:02:08.634 --> 00:02:10.534
to be arraigned
in New York City.

00:02:10.534 --> 00:02:13.200
Nothing involving the criminal
justice system is fun,

00:02:13.200 --> 00:02:14.767
especially in New York.

00:02:14.767 --> 00:02:15.968
If they told me
I won the lottery,

00:02:15.968 --> 00:02:17.534
but I have to go to
the Manhattan courthouse

00:02:17.534 --> 00:02:19.000
to pick up the check
I think,

00:02:19.000 --> 00:02:21.767
"I don't mind working."

00:02:21.767 --> 00:02:23.267
But here's one thing
I could tell you.

00:02:23.267 --> 00:02:25.567
Just as an outside observer
who has watched Donald Trump

00:02:25.567 --> 00:02:27.734
for many years now,
the man is not having fun.

00:02:27.734 --> 00:02:29.901
For one thing, he wasn't
paraded around by authorities.

00:02:29.901 --> 00:02:32.200
He mopped through the hallways
of the criminal courthouse

00:02:32.200 --> 00:02:34.300
surrounded by officers
who didn't even hold

00:02:34.300 --> 00:02:36.634
the door open for him.

00:02:36.634 --> 00:02:38.367
He had to hold the door open,

00:02:38.367 --> 00:02:40.367
and that's probably
the first time in his life

00:02:40.367 --> 00:02:41.601
he's had to do that.

00:02:41.601 --> 00:02:42.868
If Trump walked up to a door

00:02:42.868 --> 00:02:44.167
without anyone else
around to help,

00:02:44.167 --> 00:02:45.501
he'd be totally stumped.

00:02:45.501 --> 00:02:48.601
"Oh, boy. Okay, now,
what are we looking at here?

00:02:48.601 --> 00:02:50.667
I should remember this
from my real estate days.

00:02:50.667 --> 00:02:54.734
Rectangular, little shape,
tiny metallic pumpkin.

00:02:54.734 --> 00:02:57.868
Not sure what
the little pumpkin does.

00:02:57.868 --> 00:02:59.000
You know what?
I'm just going to try.

00:02:59.000 --> 00:03:01.133
Door open.
Let's see if that works.

00:03:01.133 --> 00:03:03.667
Excuse me. Excuse me, door.
You're being a very nasty door.

00:03:03.667 --> 00:03:06.067
You're a biased --
you're a biased left wing door.

00:03:06.067 --> 00:03:08.968
They gave me a Hillary door.

00:03:08.968 --> 00:03:10.133
Hashtag fake door."

00:03:10.133 --> 00:03:11.767
But when you actually
look at

00:03:11.767 --> 00:03:14.100
Donald Trump's face sitting down
in that courtroom,

00:03:14.100 --> 00:03:16.300
you can tell this is not
a man who's having fun.

00:03:16.300 --> 00:03:18.167
I mean, look at him.
That's how I look

00:03:18.167 --> 00:03:22.334
when I fall asleep on the couch
and wake up after dark.

00:03:22.334 --> 00:03:24.501
Again, it's worth
taking in this image

00:03:24.501 --> 00:03:26.334
because whatever else
you want to say about it,

00:03:26.334 --> 00:03:27.701
it's definitely historic.

00:03:27.701 --> 00:03:30.334
This is a former president
sitting in a criminal court

00:03:30.334 --> 00:03:32.200
as a defendant surrounded
by his legal team.

00:03:32.200 --> 00:03:34.701
The only thing that was missing
was a record scratch,

00:03:34.701 --> 00:03:36.167
followed by
an internal monologue.

00:03:36.167 --> 00:03:37.200
[ Record scratches ]

00:03:37.200 --> 00:03:40.267
"Yep, that's me.

00:03:40.267 --> 00:03:42.334
You're probably
wondering how I got here.

00:03:42.334 --> 00:03:47.267
Well, sit back, because
it's a pretty crazy story."

00:03:47.267 --> 00:03:49.734
[ Laughter ]

00:03:49.734 --> 00:03:53.267
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:03:53.267 --> 00:03:56.167
So Trump and his team
wanted us all to think

00:03:56.167 --> 00:03:58.567
he was enjoying the experience,
that it was fun

00:03:58.567 --> 00:04:00.868
and that it would benefit him
politically, which is BS.

00:04:00.868 --> 00:04:02.200
This is all part
of the shtick.

00:04:02.200 --> 00:04:04.267
Trump wants us to think
everything he does is by design,

00:04:04.267 --> 00:04:05.701
that it's all part
of his master plan,

00:04:05.701 --> 00:04:07.300
that he's playing
four dimensional chess

00:04:07.300 --> 00:04:08.567
and he's always getting
the best of us

00:04:08.567 --> 00:04:09.767
and he's loving
every minute of it.

00:04:09.767 --> 00:04:11.501
But it's not true.
I mean, look at him.

00:04:11.501 --> 00:04:13.868
He's used to sitting
with kings and CEOs,

00:04:13.868 --> 00:04:15.834
and now he's sitting in a chair
that five minutes

00:04:15.834 --> 00:04:18.634
before he walked in was used
by a guy who pled not guilty

00:04:18.634 --> 00:04:20.067
to one charge
of exposing himself

00:04:20.067 --> 00:04:22.534
to a squirrel in Central Park.

00:04:22.534 --> 00:04:24.901
"Sorry, Your Honor. I just
thought that squirrels liked --"

00:04:24.901 --> 00:04:28.434
"No. Will you please
advise the defendant to refrain

00:04:28.434 --> 00:04:30.000
from making jokes
about his nuts?

00:04:30.000 --> 00:04:32.968
I assure you, this being
the Manhattan Criminal Court,

00:04:32.968 --> 00:04:35.133
we've heard all
the nuts jokes before.

00:04:35.133 --> 00:04:36.934
Alright, Bailiff.
Next [bleep] case."

00:04:36.934 --> 00:04:39.434
That's just how judges
talk in New York City.

00:04:39.434 --> 00:04:41.534
[ Laughter ]

00:04:45.133 --> 00:04:46.934
Yeah, we're on the next card,
Wally.

00:04:46.934 --> 00:04:49.501
[ Laughter ]

00:04:49.501 --> 00:04:52.901
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:04:52.901 --> 00:04:55.133
Let me tell you something.
Let me tell you something.

00:04:55.133 --> 00:04:57.868
Wally -- Wally Feresten,
best in the biz.

00:04:57.868 --> 00:04:59.334
When it comes to cue cards.

00:04:59.334 --> 00:05:03.100
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:05:03.100 --> 00:05:06.334
But [bleep] crapped out here
there hard.

00:05:06.334 --> 00:05:09.033
It was a real brain freeze
by Wally.

00:05:09.033 --> 00:05:10.400
-It sounded like an ad-lib.

00:05:10.400 --> 00:05:11.567
-It sounded like an ad-lib?

00:05:11.567 --> 00:05:12.601
-Yeah, so it was so good.

00:05:12.601 --> 00:05:13.734
-All those words
were on the card, Wally.

00:05:13.734 --> 00:05:15.434
-Yeah,I know.
-You know, I don't come up

00:05:15.434 --> 00:05:17.000
with my own ideas, Wally.

00:05:17.000 --> 00:05:18.300
[ Laughter ]

00:05:18.300 --> 00:05:19.834
Sal puts them in my head.

00:05:19.834 --> 00:05:22.100
[ Laughter ]

00:05:23.834 --> 00:05:25.934
But that's why this image
is so important.

00:05:25.934 --> 00:05:28.234
It shows that even a guy
who is not too long ago,

00:05:28.234 --> 00:05:29.634
the most powerful man
in the world,

00:05:29.634 --> 00:05:31.334
the guy who controlled
our nuclear arsenal

00:05:31.334 --> 00:05:33.100
and rode around
in a presidential limo

00:05:33.100 --> 00:05:34.834
and entered every room
to hail to the chief,

00:05:34.834 --> 00:05:37.267
had to sit in that courthouse
in front of a judge

00:05:37.267 --> 00:05:39.267
just like everyone else
accused of breaking the law.

00:05:39.267 --> 00:05:40.601
In fact, if you ask me,

00:05:40.601 --> 00:05:42.501
they should have made
a real New York experience

00:05:42.501 --> 00:05:46.033
and towed his plane
while he was inside.

00:05:46.033 --> 00:05:47.968
"Rudy?

00:05:47.968 --> 00:05:49.300
Rudy, what the [bleep]?"

00:05:49.300 --> 00:05:51.200
"Sorry, boss.
I could have sworn I put enough

00:05:51.200 --> 00:05:53.434
quarters in the meter.

00:05:53.434 --> 00:05:56.234
Although they might
have been my buttons.

00:05:56.234 --> 00:06:00.300
Was getting arrested as much fun
as you thought it would be?"

00:06:00.300 --> 00:06:04.167
[ Laughing ] In fact,
he's been freaking out --

00:06:04.167 --> 00:06:05.868
"I know you
were really excited."

00:06:05.868 --> 00:06:07.634
[ Laughter ]

00:06:07.634 --> 00:06:09.501
In fact, he's been freaking out
so much that today

00:06:09.501 --> 00:06:12.000
he wrote in an all caps
social media post...

00:06:16.400 --> 00:06:18.367
It's going to be so funny
the next time a Republican tries

00:06:18.367 --> 00:06:20.267
to pretend this never happened
and claims

00:06:20.267 --> 00:06:22.400
Democrats are the ones
who want to defund the police.

00:06:22.400 --> 00:06:24.367
Joe Biden should have
this post printed out

00:06:24.367 --> 00:06:27.601
and wear it like a sandwich
board wherever he goes.

00:06:27.601 --> 00:06:29.501
"Donald Trump wants to defund
the police,

00:06:29.501 --> 00:06:32.901
and $5 footlongs,
they're back.

00:06:32.901 --> 00:06:37.634
They were gone
and I brought them back now.

00:06:37.634 --> 00:06:39.300
They're back.

00:06:39.300 --> 00:06:42.033
They're back, Jack.

00:06:42.033 --> 00:06:45.601
$5 footlong.
$5.

00:06:45.601 --> 00:06:46.901
I brought them back.

00:06:46.901 --> 00:06:49.033
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:06:49.033 --> 00:06:51.868
Chips are extra."

00:06:51.868 --> 00:06:53.501
Now, as for the merits
of the case,

00:06:53.501 --> 00:06:56.267
we did learn a lot more from
the charging document yesterday,

00:06:56.267 --> 00:06:58.434
like the fact
that Trump finalized the details

00:06:58.434 --> 00:06:59.734
of the scheme
with his fixer,

00:06:59.734 --> 00:07:01.467
Michael Cohen
in the Oval Office,

00:07:01.467 --> 00:07:02.734
or the fact that Trump

00:07:02.734 --> 00:07:04.701
also thanked another key player
in the scheme,

00:07:04.701 --> 00:07:07.100
former National Enquirer
publisher David Pecker.

00:07:07.100 --> 00:07:08.501
During his presidential
transition,

00:07:08.501 --> 00:07:10.467
invited him to both
the inauguration

00:07:10.467 --> 00:07:11.934
and dinner
at the White House.

00:07:11.934 --> 00:07:14.467
Those revelations make clear
that this is not just a case

00:07:14.467 --> 00:07:16.467
about Trump having an affair
or even paying hush money,

00:07:16.467 --> 00:07:18.634
which, if done right,
is not a crime.

00:07:18.634 --> 00:07:20.367
Despite the fact
that Trump's allies on Fox

00:07:20.367 --> 00:07:22.033
have all tried
to make it sound like this

00:07:22.033 --> 00:07:23.901
was just a silly
bookkeeping error,

00:07:23.901 --> 00:07:25.968
or that it's something that
happens all the time.

00:07:25.968 --> 00:07:29.801
You're going to break 200 years
of U.S. precedent

00:07:29.801 --> 00:07:32.767
about indicting
your political opponents

00:07:32.767 --> 00:07:35.901
over a business records charge?

00:07:35.901 --> 00:07:38.067
-We were told by the Democrats
in the media

00:07:38.067 --> 00:07:40.567
that your private life's
your private life.

00:07:40.567 --> 00:07:42.400
Everything was consensual.

00:07:42.400 --> 00:07:45.334
Now, all of a sudden,
consensual is a felony

00:07:45.334 --> 00:07:46.801
and they're literally
prosecuting

00:07:46.801 --> 00:07:48.834
the former president
over sex?

00:07:48.834 --> 00:07:51.033
-In fact, settlements like this,
whatever you think of them,

00:07:51.033 --> 00:07:52.901
are common,
both among famous people,

00:07:52.901 --> 00:07:55.601
celebrities and in
corporate America.

00:07:55.601 --> 00:07:57.701
The result is usually known
as an NDA,

00:07:57.701 --> 00:08:00.167
a non-disclosure agreement.

00:08:00.167 --> 00:08:01.334
In this case,
you can believe

00:08:01.334 --> 00:08:02.767
whatever side
you want to believe,

00:08:02.767 --> 00:08:04.934
but paying people
not to talk about things,

00:08:04.934 --> 00:08:08.734
"hush money," is ordinary in
modern America.

00:08:08.734 --> 00:08:11.100
-This must have cost the
taxpayers of New York

00:08:11.100 --> 00:08:13.501
tens of millions of dollars,

00:08:13.501 --> 00:08:16.567
the security coverage
for this situation.

00:08:16.567 --> 00:08:18.300
And you just said it.
over what?

00:08:18.300 --> 00:08:22.000
Over $130,000,
completely legal

00:08:22.000 --> 00:08:24.000
non-disclosure
agreement payment.

00:08:24.000 --> 00:08:25.601
You know, these things
happen all day,

00:08:25.601 --> 00:08:28.167
every day in the United States
of America.

00:08:28.167 --> 00:08:30.067
-That's not a defense.
That's a confession.

00:08:30.067 --> 00:08:33.234
If you think -- if you think
illegal hush money payments

00:08:33.234 --> 00:08:35.934
happen all the time,
you're telling us an awful lot

00:08:35.934 --> 00:08:38.501
about how the wealthy elite
in this country operate.

00:08:38.501 --> 00:08:39.634
"Come on, who among us

00:08:39.634 --> 00:08:41.501
has an accidentally
strangled the butler

00:08:41.501 --> 00:08:42.868
and buried them in the garden?

00:08:42.868 --> 00:08:45.334
It happens all the time.

00:08:45.334 --> 00:08:48.100
I'm on my third butler
this month."

00:08:48.100 --> 00:08:49.167
But think about that, though.

00:08:49.167 --> 00:08:50.300
They went from saying
Donald Trump

00:08:50.300 --> 00:08:51.834
is a champion
of the working class,

00:08:51.834 --> 00:08:54.400
he's fighting the establishment,
taking on the elites to saying

00:08:54.400 --> 00:08:56.234
his hush money scheme
was no big deal

00:08:56.234 --> 00:08:57.968
because rich celebrities
do it all the time.

00:08:57.968 --> 00:08:59.601
I hope Trump starts
incorporating

00:08:59.601 --> 00:09:00.868
that at his rallies.

00:09:00.868 --> 00:09:02.868
"You normies wouldn't
understand, but rich,

00:09:02.868 --> 00:09:04.033
famous guys like me,

00:09:04.033 --> 00:09:05.767
we have sex with porn stars
all the time.

00:09:05.767 --> 00:09:07.167
All the time.

00:09:07.167 --> 00:09:08.968
That's why I'm introducing
a bill to make it legal,

00:09:08.968 --> 00:09:11.133
and we're calling it
the Concealing Relationships

00:09:11.133 --> 00:09:14.601
and Monetary Enterprises Act,
aka the Crime Act.

00:09:14.601 --> 00:09:17.367
Oh, dang it.
I've -- I've done it again.

00:09:17.367 --> 00:09:19.400
Donald, you got to pay
attention to the letters.

00:09:19.400 --> 00:09:21.968
They make an acronym.
They make an acronym."

00:09:21.968 --> 00:09:23.267
But in the charging
document yesterday,

00:09:23.267 --> 00:09:24.501
the district attorney
made it clear

00:09:24.501 --> 00:09:26.634
that this case is
about a lot more

00:09:26.634 --> 00:09:28.501
than just bookkeeping
or a sex scandal.

00:09:28.501 --> 00:09:30.000
Trump funneled money
from his business

00:09:30.000 --> 00:09:32.400
to a fixer to silence
an adult film star weeks

00:09:32.400 --> 00:09:33.767
before an election
to help his campaign

00:09:33.767 --> 00:09:35.567
and become the most
powerful man in the world.

00:09:35.567 --> 00:09:37.868
It was a plot to hide
information from the public

00:09:37.868 --> 00:09:39.467
and affect the outcome
of an election.

00:09:39.467 --> 00:09:41.067
And by the way,
who knows if it would have?

00:09:41.067 --> 00:09:43.300
Probably not. He probably could
have done a campaign event

00:09:43.300 --> 00:09:45.667
in the lobby of the hotel
where he had the affair

00:09:45.667 --> 00:09:48.167
and his supporters would have
still lined up to take selfies.

00:09:48.167 --> 00:09:50.701
"I'm going to head up
to the room now any minute,

00:09:50.701 --> 00:09:52.100
and then any minute after that,

00:09:52.100 --> 00:09:55.567
I'll be right back down
to tell you how it went.

00:09:55.567 --> 00:09:57.968
I don't think you'll have time
to run to the bathroom.

00:09:57.968 --> 00:10:00.367
I'd stick around."

00:10:00.367 --> 00:10:01.834
After his court appearance
yesterday,

00:10:01.834 --> 00:10:04.033
Trump flew back to Mar-a-Lago
to give a speech to supporters

00:10:04.033 --> 00:10:05.901
where he whined
about the usual bull[bleep]

00:10:05.901 --> 00:10:08.334
